{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788370855,"nonce":"40AUZa06kLgH1n1MW6MngI8Rwl8=","message":"Partially answered by the naming-dialog fix (`5cb1f9f`, shipped 2026-09-02), and the open question this issue's Open-questions section raised is RESOLVED against the source.\n\n**The trigger IS a readable predicate**, not a schedule. `RimWorld/NamePlayerFactionAndSettlementUtility`:\n\n    private static bool CanNameFaction(int ticksPassed)\n        =\u003e !Faction.OfPlayer.HasName \u0026\u0026 (float)ticksPassed / 60000f \u003e= 4.3f \u0026\u0026 CanNameAnythingNow();\n\n    private static bool CanNameSettlement(Settlement fb, int ticksPassed)\n        =\u003e fb.Faction == Faction.OfPlayer \u0026\u0026 !fb.namedByPlayer \u0026\u0026 (float)ticksPassed / 60000f \u003e= 4.3f\n           \u0026\u0026 fb.HasMap \u0026\u0026 fb.Map.dangerWatcher.DangerRating != StoryDanger.High\n           \u0026\u0026 fb.Map.mapPawns.FreeColonistsSpawnedCount != 0 \u0026\u0026 CanNameAnythingNow();\n\nwith `ticksPassed` = `TicksGame` for the faction and `TicksGame - factionBase.creationGameTicks` for the settlement, and\n\n    CanNameAnythingNow() =\u003e AnyPlayerHomeMap != null \u0026\u0026 CurrentMap != null \u0026\u0026 CurrentMap.IsPlayerHome\n                            \u0026\u0026 !GameEnder.gameEnding\n                            \u0026\u0026 (some home map has \u003e= 2 spawned free colonists)\n                            \u0026\u0026 (some home map has no active threat to the player)\n\n`Faction.FactionTick` evaluates it on `TicksGame % 1000 == 200 \u0026\u0026 IsPlayer`. So item 1 is cleanly specifiable: `HasName` and `namedByPlayer` are the pending booleans, the 4.3-day thresholds give a *tick* the step falls due, and `CanNameAnythingNow`'s clauses say which of them is currently BLOCKING it — which is the more useful read, since a colony under threat or below two colonists has the step pending and un-raisable. There is also a `CanName*Soon` pair (`+30000` ticks) the game uses to decide whether to offer the combined dialog; a `soon` boolean is free.\n\nDo NOT infer any of it from the name string — the issue said so and the source agrees: `HasName` is the test, not `Name != null`.\n\n**What the fix already covers.** Item 2's second half: `checklists/triggered.md` gains a `colony-naming` trigger, and it carries this issue's actual lesson — a checklist section that closes before its work falls due hides that work forever. `playbook/PLAY-LOOP.md`'s dialog rule gains the case. The agent no longer meets the window cold either: `interactions` and the halt payload report `kind:\"name-entry\"` with the pre-filled values, and the advance loop accepts it automatically so it does not halt at all.\n\n**What is still owed here: item 1, the observation surface.** `digest`/`status` still say nothing about a pending naming step, so an agent cannot see it coming — only that it has been handled after the fact (an `action` row, `verb: dialog-accept`, `via: auto`). That is a smaller gap now that the halt is gone, and it is the difference between a scheduled item and a silently-handled interrupt. Item 3's acceptance stands as written.\n\nGrep note from the original filing still holds: no observer reads `HasName` or `namedByPlayer`; the only `settlement` references in the source are `TradeVerbs` and `QuestVerbs` ruling world settlements out of scope.","files":null}]}